From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:36:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] cts: connect every sink when two share a location
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

HTreeBuilder found a clock sink by its location: mapLocationToSink_ held
one sink per location, and a second sink at the same point overwrote the
first. Two registers placed on top of each other (same master, location
and orientation, so the same clock pin point) then resolved to one
ClockInst. Sink clustering put that one into its cluster's subnet twice,
and so did the leaf level of a tree too small to cluster; the other
register was in no subnet. Writing the tree takes every sink off the
clock net and connects only the subnets' sinks, so its clock pin was
left on no net. Nothing said so: CTS-0035 counts locations and reported
every sink covered.

On a large hierarchical design (XiangShan's XSTile Top, in bazel-orfs) a
global placement left 7 pairs of registers at identical locations, and
CTS left 7 registers unclocked; CTS, global route and the routed checks
passed, and only a later check of the clock found them.

Sink clustering now takes each sink by its index in the vector that runs
parallel to its points, instead of looking its location up. The map
keeps every sink at a location, and the leaf level connects the next one
each time the location appears among its branches' sinks. Once the
subnets are made, a sink that is in none of them is an error (CTS-0138)
instead of a clock pin left on no net. #9816 nudged cloned clock gaters
apart by 1 dbu for the same map; sinks that already shared a location
when CTS started were still lost.

Where no two sinks share a location, the trees are the same: on the
reproducer's controls and on a small hierarchical design, the databases
written after CTS were byte-identical with and without the change.

colocated_registers puts a register on top of another in a clustered
tree (226 sinks) and in one too small to cluster (37 sinks). It fails
without the change (ffa_twin's clock pin on no net) and passes with it.

Carried in bazel-orfs, not upstreamed; retires with the //:bump onto an
OpenROAD that has it. Upstream candidate: a bugfix.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
